Z||000000||sluppy123||01-24-2001||08:50 PM||||Are you tired of that plain looking Upper engine strut (AKA Dog bone) Don't like the looks of Fiero Stores "Ultimate" Dog bone? Maybe you need on of these.<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11170243&p=39044910&Sequence=0">    <P>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11170243&p=39044604&Sequence=0">   <P>Each dogbone is cut from a solid chunk of Aluminum Alloy, fitted with a press fit steel bushing, Then polished to a mirror shine. Price $50+ shipping anywhere in the US.<P>If anybodys interested I can make one for the V-6 or 4 cyl , (even a custom length for you engine swap)<P>Here's some pic of them installed<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11170243&p=39035603&Sequence=0">    <P>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11170243&p=39034910&Sequence=0">    <P>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11170243&p=39035930&Sequence=0">    <P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered and On The Bottle<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=7653930&p=37756786&Sequence=0">    <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by sluppy123 (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Black88GT||01-24-2001||08:55 PM||||Call me crazy, but shouldn't it have bushings?||||reg||5
Z||000002||fieroshop||01-25-2001||11:07 AM||||Sluppy, this dogbone that you are making looks nice but has a flaw as well as the ultimate dogbone.<BR> I have found that Fieros having the ultimate dogbone in time has to have the mounting brackets replaced due to very little give and something has to give as the engine rocks back and forth. Hence I do not recommend your dogbone nor the ultimate dogbone to anybody.<BR>A oem dogbone has rubber bushings and is cheaper to replace then having to replace the mounting brackets.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-26-2001||01:39 AM||||VERY NICE LOOKING..... and a great price I think!!!  Sluppy...  Is there any way for you to design it where the wholes are LARGER for the use of *Poly* bushing's???  This would be a hit IF ..... you can do that.<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Greg Piet||01-26-2001||11:22 AM||||Uhhh looks like I would need to go with aluminum bushings all around if I were to do that... besides I would have to go race against meaner faster cars with those dang fangled V8's where I only have a V6 just for a metal bushing material.  But it shore is purdy!||||reg||1
Z||000005||sluppy123||01-26-2001||05:23 PM||||I've used a solid alum dogbone for the past 3 years with no problem but I DO see Fieroshops point. However if your using poly motor mounts all around there's really no point in having a upper mount using rubber, is there?.<P> As far as the size of the hole, I can do any size out there. currently I'm making some bushings out of various materials and am going to give them a try. I could even make the holes the same as the ultimate dogbone so the poly bushings could be used.||||reg||1
